# Red Cabbage Breakfast Hash

Based on [https://www.thekitchn.com/cabbage-hash-recipe-23265895](https://www.thekitchn.com/cabbage-hash-recipe-23265895) (wayback unavailable)

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 2 Tbsp [Olive Oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } or Butter
- [ ] 1 medium [Onion]{ ing="onion" }, diced
- [ ] 2 cloves [Garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 2 medium [Potatoes]{ ing="potatoes" }, diced into 1/2 inch cubes
- [ ] 1/4 head [Red Cabbage]{ ing="red-cabbage" }, thinly sliced (about 2-3 cups)
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [Paprika]{ ing="paprika" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [Salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [Black Pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
- [ ] (Optional) 4 [Eggs]{ ing="egg" } for topping
- [ ] (Optional) Fresh [herbs like Parsley]{ ing="herbs-like-parsley" } or Chives for garnish
- [ ] (Optional) [Hot sauce]{ ing="hot-sauce" } for serving

## Recipe

1. Heat 1 Tbsp [oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } in a large skillet over medium-high heat
1. Add diced [potatoes]{ ing="potatoes" } and cook for 8-10 minutes, stirring occasionally, until golden and tender
1. Push potatoes to the side and add remaining 1 Tbsp oil
1. Add [onion]{ ing="onion" } and cook for 3-4 minutes until softened
1. Add [garlic]{ ing="garlic" } and cook for 30 seconds until fragrant
1. Add sliced [red cabbage]{ ing="red-cabbage" }, [paprika]{ ing="paprika" }, [salt]{ ing="salt" }, and [pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }. Stir everything together
1. Cook for 5-7 minutes, stirring occasionally, until cabbage is tender and lightly caramelized
1. If using [eggs]{ ing="egg" }, make 4 wells in the hash and crack an egg into each well
1. Cover and cook for 3-5 minutes until eggs are set to your liking
1. Garnish with fresh herbs and serve with [hot sauce]{ ing="hot-sauce" } if desired

## Notes

- Sweet potatoes work well as a substitute for regular potatoes
- Add cooked sausage or bacon for extra protein
- Can meal prep the hash without eggs and reheat throughout the week
- The red cabbage will turn a beautiful purple color as it cooks
